Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.

ABOUT&nbsp; THE JOB &nbsp;

We are&nbsp;seeking&nbsp;a highly motivated&nbsp; Configuration Design Engineer &nbsp;for our Air Dominance &amp; Strike hardware engineering organization. In this role, you will&nbsp;be responsible for&nbsp;the early-stage conceptual layout, sizing, and multi-disciplinary vehicle design of next-generation Group 5 Unmanned Aerial Systems (UAS) and advanced missile platforms. Operating at the front end of our development cycle, you will bridge the gap between high-level mission requirements and physical execution, turning "clean sheet" concepts into optimized, flight-ready configurations in record time. &nbsp;

WHAT YOU’LL DO &nbsp;

• Lead and execute the physical layout, sizing, and configuration design of new air vehicles and missile systems from concept to preliminary design. &nbsp;

• Develop parametric CAD models, complex surface models, and high-fidelity Outer Mold Line (OML) and Inner Mold Line (IML) lofts using NX&nbsp;pdf. &nbsp;

• Conduct rapid multi-disciplinary trade studies to evaluate engine selection,&nbsp;propulsion path integration, planform geometry, control effector layouts, structural joints, landing gear, and weapons integration. &nbsp;

• Drive spatial integration across subsystem teams, managing keep-in/keep-out zones for avionics, fuel, and payload systems. &nbsp;

• Support downstream engineering analyses by&nbsp;providing clean surface models&nbsp;optimized&nbsp;for Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD), Finite Element Analysis (FEA), and Electromagnetic (RF/IR signature) evaluations. &nbsp;

• Incorporate survivability principles into early-stage designs,&nbsp;optimizing&nbsp;vehicle shaping, transitions, gaps, and treatments for RF and IR signature reduction. &nbsp;

• Estimate mass&nbsp;properties, center of gravity (CG), and stability margins. &nbsp;

• Partner with Chief Engineers, systems engineers, and customers to translate operational requirements into elegant, affordable, and mission-capable design concepts. &nbsp;

REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS &nbsp;

• Bachelor of Science degree in Aerospace, Mechanical Engineering, or a related technical field. &nbsp;

• 5+ years of experience in conceptual or preliminary design of&nbsp;aircraft, unmanned aerial systems (UAS), or missile systems. &nbsp;

• Strong, hands-on&nbsp;proficiency&nbsp;in 3D parametric CAD modeling and advanced surfacing (Siemens NX&nbsp;preferred&nbsp;,&nbsp;CATIA, or Creo). &nbsp;

• Demonstrated experience executing multi-disciplinary trade studies covering aerodynamics,&nbsp;propulsion integration, structures, and mass&nbsp;properties. &nbsp;

• Proven ability to work in rapid development,&nbsp;prototyping, or "Skunk Works" style engineering environments. &nbsp;

• Excellent communication, presentation, and collaboration skills, with the ability to lead cross-functional technical reviews. &nbsp;

• Must be&nbsp;eligible&nbsp;to obtain and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;a U.S. Secret Security Clearance. &nbsp;

